+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional ``canonical`` option describes the
+   type represented by the alias and is displayed in the signature after ``=``.
+   The directive may also contain a description body.
+
+   For example::
+
+      .. py:type:: UserId
+         :canonical: int
+
+         Identifier assigned to a user.
+
+   The alias can be declared at module level or inside a class description. A
+   class-scoped alias is qualified by its class name.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical: represented type
+      :type: Python annotation
+
+      Describe the type represented by the alias. The expression is parsed as
+      an annotation, so referenced types can be cross-referenced.
+
